RISC3D test kit 28 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 27's results: every texture reads back from the GPU exactly as
TORCS uploaded it, and the GPU's test cards match software's. So the
GPU stores and draws the textures right, as long as nothing else is
switched on. The fault comes from something TORCS has switched on
while drawing: fog, lighting or colour material.

This kit's rol-3d (0.16) redraws your recording on the GPU with each
of those left off in turn. The picture where the car's livery comes
back names the cause.

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 27.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.16-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240

